Z||000000||loafer87gt||02-19-2001||08:50 PM||||I am trying to through together a website and thought I'd get some feedback from you guys before I progress any further. The main problem I am finding with HTML stuff is that it may look great on one machine, but if someone is running low colors or a different resolution on their monitor things start to get distorted. The site right now is using a lot of animated GIF's so it is probably slow as heck on a dialup connection. I am going to try and optimize it so that it loads better for the bandwidth impaired  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Also, does anyone know an HTML code to turn off the toolbars and shrink the icons for the main window like hitting the F11 key in Explorer does? I find the page looks a lot better when the F11 key is hit before navigating... Anyways, its a start for the site, the art stuff in the Gallery is a couple years old and over the February break I'm gonna scan in some of my sketches, renderings, and paintings. If any of you guys have any artwork you would like to share on the site, drop me a line and I'll put you in the virtual gallery!<P>Oh almost forgot, the url is...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.verylittlebrain.com/loafer" TARGET=_blank>www.verylittlebrain.com/loafer</A> <P>||||reg||1
